d of a disembodied floating appendage.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/22fbf814-5fbd-403d-8f95-0a6e4dae31d5.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Cancel Anti Wokeflake Snow Culture (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"8 October-8 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/22fbf814-5fbd-403d-8f95-0a6e4dae31d5-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"19401AJHGNGSSNHVHGVRMMRHQDRBGPQPM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-08T20:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-08T19:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-08T20:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-08T19:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"around 60min/PG - by PlainesPlough - It’ll be everything you know and love them for: championing artists, bringing creative people together, and telling bold new stories on the stage.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/b26f78d8-1bb6-4f4e-8bed-5f63a41bc31c.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Come to Where I Am (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"9 October-9 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/b26f78d8-1bb6-4f4e-8bed-5f63a41bc31c-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"18601AGJVHRJDDNTMMMDTKPLTNBGVTLHV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-09T18:40:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-09T17:40:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-09T18:40:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-09T17:40:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"1hr/15+ by Stephen Christopher and Graeme Smith - Donny’s life has been shaped by addiction and isolation, but an unexpected friendship begins to change everything. A joyful and deeply moving story about connection, recovery and the courage to let yourself be seen.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/ebec8350-01df-472e-b785-96dc7e3843e1.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dancing Shoes (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"30 September-30 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/ebec8350-01df-472e-b785-96dc7e3843e1-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"20801AJMTLQPSPKJDPVTSBMNNJNRPTPVH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-30T18:40:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-30T17:40:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-30T18:40:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-30T17:40:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"Featuring Lashana Lynch, dissent is an explosive new play from debbie tucker green, one of the most distinctive and influential voices in contemporary British theatre. Running time: TBC.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/609048dc-a52e-4ba8-a5be-465512ac1684.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"DISSENT","instanceDates":"5 March-24 April","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/609048dc-a52e-4ba8-a5be-465512ac1684-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"24601AQBNLBQCHKVGDVHQJVMMGKLGNBDJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-05T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-05T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-24T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-24T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Genre":"New writing - star casting","attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":"2026-10-06T00:00:00","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":"2026-10-01T00:00:00","attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":"2026-10-05T00:00:00","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"Main House","attribute_Festival":""},{"description":"","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\tBuy your <span class=\"BoldText\"><span class=\"ItalicText\">dissent</span> programme</span> in advance for £5 and save £1. Programmes cost £6 at the venue. You will receive a voucher which you can exchange for your programme at the box office when you visit the theatre.<span><br/></span> <span><br/></span><img src=\"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/a2420a8e-cb85-4797-aee6-cc563670d844.jpg\" />\r\n</div>","duration":0,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/a2420a8e-cb85-4797-aee6-cc563670d844.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"dissent programme","instanceDates":"11 March-24 April","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/a2420a8e-cb85-4797-aee6-cc563670d844-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"26601APLTNSPSGDPBRQVGGSRDMVBVVNQK","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-03-11T19:00:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-03-11T19:00:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-04-24T19:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-04-24T18:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Genre":"New writing - star casting","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":true,"attribute_Venue":"Main House","attribute_Festival":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"What happens when an unstoppable force (one man's vanity) meets an immovable object (Catholicism)?\r\n\r\nFind out in the Edinburgh Comedy Award nominated debut hour of standup from one of the UK's most exciting young comedians, fresh from his sold out run at Edinburgh Fringe Festival. Dom McGovern is the co-writer of Chicken Shop Date, a BBC New Comedy Award Nominee, and has been on tour supporting Aisling Bea, Olga Koch, Sophie Duker, and Urooj Ashfaq.\r\n\r\n'Endlessly entertaining and outrageously funny' - Rolling Stone\r\n'Brilliant and Hilarious' - Rosie Jones\r\n'Born to be a comedian. A fizzing, hilarious superstar' - Aisling Bea\r\n'Gaggy' - Chortle\r\n\r\n5 stars - Three Weeks\r\n4 stars - Chortle, The Skinny, One4Review\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dom McGovern: Prize Hog (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"19 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"23601ABQMTDMTTDQVVNJCNJPSQCSVMLHB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T20:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T19:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T20:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T19:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_Genre":"Studio","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"50min/15+ - by Sabrina Mahfouz - Not (just) a strip club exposé. It’s a story of a young woman trying to find her place in the world. It is also quite funny. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":50,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/ec17f070-3b8f-44ef-9252-e2622721b249.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Dry Ice (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"29 September-29 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/ec17f070-3b8f-44ef-9252-e2622721b249-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"18201AHGNDCRVCPJBPPJCHBJKBJSRNNKN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-29T18:40:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-29T17:40:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-29T18:40:00","lastInstan