e Tate\" ★★★★★ - Fourth Wall\r\n★★★★★ - The Wee Review\r\n★★★★★ - Theatre Weekly\r\n★★★★★ - Fringefeed\r\n★★★★★ - The Scoop\r\n★★★★★ - Scenestr\r\n★★★★★ - The Recs\r\n★★★★ - The Stage\r\nWinner: Best Theatre, Adelaide Fringe 2026\r\n\r\nFollowing a sell-out 2026 Edinburgh Fringe run, this will be a special one night only presentation, reimagined for Shedinburgh.\r\n","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/2ceae352-dd66-4359-84af-c52b34ccbf7f.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Kirsty Mann: Corpse (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"19 September-19 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/2ceae352-dd66-4359-84af-c52b34ccbf7f-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"23401AHHMQSVVPPKJGSDQCLPJRGKVPLMQ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T15:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T14:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-19T15:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-19T14:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_Genre":"Studio","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"Tiago Rodrigues’s La Distance is a breathtakingly beautiful and profoundly human production about separation, hope, and the bond between parent and child. Performed in French, with English surtitles. Running time: 1 hour 30 mins, no interval.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":90,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/a98595d7-5097-407a-8381-2a582942c58e.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"LA DISTANCE","instanceDates":"22 January-13 February","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/a98595d7-5097-407a-8381-2a582942c58e-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"10201AJHJGJMTBHDNGMTSMTVVGPNSHHLL","firstInstanceDateTime":"2027-01-22T19:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-01-22T19:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2027-02-13T14:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2027-02-13T14:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Genre":"New writing","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"Main House","attribute_Festival":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"1hr/18+ - Lucy McCormick queer cabaret spectacular. In a despairing world, Lucy attempts to create community and connection through pole dancing, cat impersonation, a clairvoyant and some quick re-working of social policy. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/0ea2be67-7c3e-4f0f-801e-a3c86b8db619.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Lucy & Friends (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"22 September-23 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/0ea2be67-7c3e-4f0f-801e-a3c86b8db619-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"16601ARPMPTNDDCJCLRDPBTPKBJMLVCDR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-22T20:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-22T19:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-23T20:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-23T19:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_Genre":"Studio","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"1hr/18+ - Written by an anonymous woman. Performed by an unprepared man. A funny and frank insight into heterosexual female desire, read out loud by a male comic.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/f3258b5a-e0f2-425b-8c16-67744e44f344.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Manwatching (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"10 October-10 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/f3258b5a-e0f2-425b-8c16-67744e44f344-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"17801ANDDGKKLBMPBRRTQKGLNDCMQGQHV","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T16:50:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T15:50:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T16:50:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T15:50:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"55 min/PG - Four time Fringe First winner Gary McNair returns with his 5 star tribute to Scotland’s alternative bard. It’s the incredible true story of ‘the world’s worst poet’. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":55,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/99abcf2b-fb35-4223-bf14-491a145d0259.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"McGonagall's Chronicles (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"20 September-20 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/99abcf2b-fb35-4223-bf14-491a145d0259-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"21001AHGQKHHCBJDNTTTMDTTPLSBDJSQB","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-20T15:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-20T14:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-20T15:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-20T14:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"15+ 1hr - Nina and Monkey talking raw in a room about whatever comes to mind. Nina enjoys talking to monkey but feels she needs an excuse to do so. Monkey resents only existing onstage. This podcast solves both of their problems.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/d6bc8407-9526-45dc-b4a4-5e12d4d08534.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Nina Conti: Nina and Monkey's Podcast (WIP) (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"3 October-3 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/d6bc8407-9526-45dc-b4a4-5e12d4d08534-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"25001ADDVSKQBVSNBTBDPCMQTVGBHJDPN","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T15:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T14:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T15:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T14:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"1hr10 min/12+ - Wright&Grainger - A remarkable retelling of an Ancient Greek myth using live music and spoken word about how far you'd go for the ones who mean the most.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":70,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/b91aa76c-943c-4b52-be1e-fd87d7666fa3.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Orpheus (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"26 September-26 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/b91aa76c-943c-4b52-be1e-fd87d7666fa3-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"14002AJLHTMKCRKHSQMKRQLMBKPQPVQDP","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-26T13:40:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-26T12:40:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-26T13:40:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-26T12:40:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_Genre":"Studio","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"With 20+ five-star reviews, the Multi-Award winning POLICE COPS bring you the show that started it all! Reloaded and supercharged for 2026, expect adrenaline-fuelled physical comedy, 80s bangers, and uncompromising facial hair.\r\n\r\nWinner: STAGE AWARD FOR ACTING EXCELLENCE \u2028\r\nWinner: BEST SHOW, Toronto Fringe\u2028\r\nWINNER: BEST INTERNATIONAL SHOW, Cape Town Fringe\r\nWINNER: BRIGHTON FRINGE AWARD FOR EXCELLENCE\u2028\r\n\r\n★★★★★ WhatsOnStage\r\n★★★★★ The Stage\r\n★★★★★ Theatre Weekly\r\n\r\n'It's hip, radical, funny as f*ck and a work of towering genius' Bill Nighy \r\n'It takes brains to be this dumb!' Stewart Lee\r\nThis will be a special stripped-back version of the hit comedy show, reimagined for Shedinburgh.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":55,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/f9f3c370-3ff3-40ce-bf4a-7b6ea0c796b0.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Police Cops: The Original (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"10 October-10 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/f9f3c370-3ff3-40ce-bf4a-7b6ea0c796b0-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"23801AJTHHRQPTBGSQKNGJHMKGQMHTHHM","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T21:30:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T20:30:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T21:30:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T20:30:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_Genre":"Studio","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"1hr - 14+ - This show is a story about a time when Rob Auton had a job as an estate agent on the planet Jupiter. It is fiction.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rob Auton: JUPITER (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"10 October-10 October","thumbnailUrl":"","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"24401ANRSMNVVNPTCKDHLSQSTGQBDDKHJ","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T15:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T14:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T15:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T14:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_Genre":"Studio","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"1hr - 15+ - By Molly Windust. ‘The Woman’ is unhappily married and harbouring a secret. When her in-laws suddenly die, she struggles to cope with her grieving husband, and begins hoarding seaside themed objects in their bedroom. As the room fills with taxidermy seals, shells and quite a few fish, her marriage  disintegrates and she must come to terms with a loss of her own.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/fb81bf5d-8f80-49af-9118-f9e9e39712ce.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Rockpools (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"2 October-3 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/fb81bf5d-8f80-49af-9118-f9e9e39712ce-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"24201AQBJSCTMKBQRHSLCPQSBDTRMBNBT","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-02T20:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-02T19:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-03T20:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-03T19:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_Genre":"Studio","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"55 min/12+ - by Hayley Canham. This is the untold story of Sappho — poetess, queer icon, and history's first great songwriter. A musical memoir of women who dare to love, to dream, and to create in defiance of the world.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":55,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/3145c328-acfb-4ab7-8302-1265de8053dd.jpg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sappho: The Poetess (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"27 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/3145c328-acfb-4ab7-8302-1265de8053dd-thumbnail.jpg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"21201ARBBTMBLNJJTVHKLSDDJRJTLMNRD","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-27T13:40:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-27T12:40:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-27T13:40:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-27T12:40:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"50min/15+ - by Bryony Kimmings - Following an STI diagnosis, Bryony retraces her chaotic romantic history in this hilarious and heartfelt journey through sex, love and self-discovery while blending cabaret, comedy, dance, song and raw storytelling.","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":50,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/049069fa-cbb3-4cf7-9198-b2a4d00c311f.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Sex Idiot (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"9 October-10 October","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/049069fa-cbb3-4cf7-9198-b2a4d00c311f-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"18802ATHHKJHPRCCSSHPGMHJGNTGBBKNH","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-09T20:10:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-09T19:10:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-10-10T20:10:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-10-10T19:10:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"1hr/15+ - by Marjolein Robertson. A Shetland story steeped in both historic truth and elements of myth. Set in the days of the Norse, following Auslag, the daughter of the Jarl who becomes an outcast in her own community. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":60,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/5a39f530-10b7-467f-9db4-68b3750c761e.jpeg","isOnSale":true,"name":"Shetland Nordic Saga (Shedinburgh)","instanceDates":"27 September-27 September","thumbnailUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/5a39f530-10b7-467f-9db4-68b3750c761e-thumbnail.jpeg","webUrl":"","webEventId":null,"id":"19001AGPSVSHKKJGHGMBKJNKLNQCSNLPR","firstInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-27T16:50:00","firstInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-27T15:50:00Z","lastInstanceDateTime":"2026-09-27T16:50:00","lastInstanceDateTimeUtc":"2026-09-27T15:50:00Z","altText":"","attribute_Festival":"Shedinburgh","attribute_SupplementaryEvent":false,"attribute_Venue":"The Maria Theatre","attribute_Genre":"","attribute_PriorityBookingPatronsStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingSoulmatesStarts":null,"attribute_PriorityBookingFriendsStarts":null},{"description":"2hrs/All ages - Lineup: TAZ, Tom Bright, and Heidi Boulali.\r\n\r\nFounder Rafe Offer swapped a noisy Soho pub for a living room gig. The idea: a quiet room, a present audience and really great live music. Sofar London has hosted countless artists early in their careers, including Olivia Dean, Hozier, Tom Odell,  Emeli Sandé, Wolf Alice, Bastille, Lianne La Havas, George Ezra, Jorja Smith, Kae Tempest, and Lola Young. ","htmlDescription":"<div id>\r\n\r\n</div>","duration":120,"imageUrl":"https://system.spektrix.com/youngvic/files/cc9bf843-9ebc-40be-9b4a-fe417cee96e7.jpeg","isOnS